{"body": "This article relates to the Pennsylvania Child and Dependent Care Enhancement Tax Credit Program.\n(1601-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1601-W", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w/section-1601-w", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2024-01-03", "heading": "Scope of article", "id": "f508cf65-c14c-56a1-8b31-38f2731d9264", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W", "pennsylvania:section": "1601-W", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1601-W"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1601-W", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W", "display_number": "1601-W", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "source_history": ["(1601-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)"]}, "ordinal": 1, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "parent_id": "00e7ba89-cea0-58e7-848b-416e03e5a9cc", "source_as_of": "2024-01-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1601-W", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "The following words and phrases when used in this article shall have the meanings given to them in this section unless the context clearly indicates otherwise:\n\"Applicable percent.\" As defined in section 21(a)(2) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 in effect for the taxable year beginning after December 31, 2021, and ending before January 1, 2023.\n\"Department.\" The Department of Revenue of the Commonwealth.\n\"Employment-related expenses.\" As defined in section 21(b)(2) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986.\n\"Internal Revenue Code of 1986.\" The Internal Revenue Code of 1986 (Public Law 99-514, 26 U.S.C. \u00a7 1 et seq.).\n\"Qualifying individual.\" As defined in section 21(b)(1) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986.\n\"Resident individual.\" An individual who meets any of the following criteria:\n(1) Is domiciled in this Commonwealth, unless the individual maintains no permanent place of abode in this Commonwealth and does maintain a permanent place of abode elsewhere and spends in the aggregate no more than 30 days of the taxable year in this Commonwealth.\n(2) Is not domiciled in this Commonwealth, but maintains a permanent place of abode in this Commonwealth and spends in the aggregate more than 183 days of the taxable year in this Commonwealth.\n\"Section 21 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986.\" Section 21 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 (Public Law 99-514, 26 U.S.C. \u00a7 21).\n\"Tax credit.\" The Pennsylvania child and dependent care enhancement tax credit provided for under this article.\n\"Tax liability.\" The liability for taxes imposed under Article III of the Tax Reform Code of 1971, excluding any tax withheld by an employer under Article III of the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n\"Tax Reform Code of 1971.\" The act of March 4, 1971 (P.L.6, No.2), known as the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n\"Taxable year.\" As defined in section 301 of the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n\"Taxpayer.\" A resident individual subject to the tax imposed under Article III of the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n(1602-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)\nCompiler's Note: See section 34(6)(i) of Act 34 of 2023 in the appendix to this act for special provisions relating to continuation of prior law.", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1602-W", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w/section-1602-w", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2024-01-03", "heading": "Definitions", "id": "6c812a60-efc7-5a31-8b6a-4768af396ae2", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W", "pennsylvania:section": "1602-W", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1602-W"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1602-W", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W", "display_number": "1602-W", "kind": "section", "notes": ["Compiler's Note: See section 34(6)(i) of Act 34 of 2023 in the appendix to this act for special provisions relating to continuation of prior law."], "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "source_history": ["(1602-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)"]}, "ordinal": 2, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "parent_id": "00e7ba89-cea0-58e7-848b-416e03e5a9cc", "source_as_of": "2024-01-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1602-W", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "(a) Tax credit.--For taxable years beginning after December 31, 2021, a taxpayer who receives a credit under section 21 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 may claim a tax credit against the taxpayer's tax liability.\n(b) Amount of tax credit.--The amount of the tax credit under subsection (a) for the taxable year beginning after December 31, 2021, and ending before January 1, 2023, shall be equal to 30% of:\n(1) the actual amount of employment-related expenses incurred by the taxpayer and claimed for the Federal tax credit under section 21 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 during the prior taxable year or the following, as applicable, whichever is less:\n(i) $3,000 for one qualifying individual with respect to the taxpayer; or\n(ii) $6,000 for two or more qualifying individuals with respect to the taxpayer; multiplied by\n(2) the applicable percent, with respect to the taxpayer, in effect for the taxable year beginning after December 31, 2021, and ending before January 1, 2023.\n(c) Amount of tax credit in subsequent taxable years.--The amount of the tax credit under subsection (a) for taxable years beginning after December 31, 2022, and for each taxable year thereafter, shall be equal to 100% of:\n(1) the actual amount of employment-related expenses incurred by the taxpayer and claimed for the Federal tax credit under section 21 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 during the prior taxable year or the following, as applicable, whichever is less:\n(i) $3,000 for one qualifying individual with respect to the taxpayer; or\n(ii) $6,000 for two or more qualifying individuals with respect to the taxpayer; multiplied by\n(2) the applicable percent, with respect to the taxpayer, in effect for the taxable year beginning after December 31, 2021, and ending before January 1, 2023.\n(d) Claim of tax credit.--A taxpayer shall claim a tax credit under this section on a return filed under section 330 of the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n(e) Applicability of tax credit.--The tax credit under this section shall be applied against the taxpayer's tax liability. If the tax credit exceeds the taxpayer's tax liability, the department may issue a refund under the procedures specified in section 346 of the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n(1603-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)\nCompiler's Note: See section 34(6)(ii) of Act 34 of 2023 in the appendix to this act for special provisions relating to continuation of prior law.", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1603-W", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w/section-1603-w", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2024-01-03", "heading": "Credit for child and dependent care employment-related expenses", "id": "b6fee4a5-3670-554e-9dcd-0c2ec45cc535", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W", "pennsylvania:section": "1603-W", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1603-W"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1603-W", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W", "display_number": "1603-W", "kind": "section", "notes": ["Compiler's Note: See section 34(6)(ii) of Act 34 of 2023 in the appendix to this act for special provisions relating to continuation of prior law."], "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "source_history": ["(1603-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)"]}, "ordinal": 3, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "parent_id": "00e7ba89-cea0-58e7-848b-416e03e5a9cc", "source_as_of": "2024-01-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1603-W", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "The following apply:\n(1) A taxpayer is not entitled to carry over, carry back or sell, assign or transfer a tax credit under this article.\n(2) A taxpayer may not claim a tax credit for the same employment-related expenses used to claim a tax credit on a return filed by another taxpayer.\n(1604-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1604-W", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w/section-1604-w", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2024-01-03", "heading": "Prohibitions", "id": "5192dae0-500a-524d-aecb-eb1a30600b9e", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W", "pennsylvania:section": "1604-W", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1604-W"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1604-W", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W", "display_number": "1604-W", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "source_history": ["(1604-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)"]}, "ordinal": 4, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "parent_id": "00e7ba89-cea0-58e7-848b-416e03e5a9cc", "source_as_of": "2024-01-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1604-W", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "The provisions of section 21 of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 in effect as of July 8, 2022, and any Federal regulations promulgated regarding those provisions, shall apply to the department's interpretation and administration of the tax credit provided for under this article.\n(1605-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1605-W", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w/section-1605-w", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2024-01-03", "heading": "Application of Internal Revenue Code of 1986", "id": "42d316ea-6420-500e-9978-2b3922b9f616", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W", "pennsylvania:section": "1605-W", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1605-W"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1605-W", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W", "display_number": "1605-W", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "source_history": ["(1605-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)"]}, "ordinal": 5, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "parent_id": "00e7ba89-cea0-58e7-848b-416e03e5a9cc", "source_as_of": "2024-01-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1605-W", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "The department may jointly administer this article with the Tax Reform Code of 1971, including joint reporting of information, forms, returns, statements, documents or other information submitted to the department.\n(1605.1-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)\nCompiler's Note: See section 34(6)(ii) of Act 34 of 2023 in the appendix to this act for special provisions relating to continuation of prior law.", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1605.1-W", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w/section-1605.1-w", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2024-01-03", "heading": "Administration of article", "id": "1fc06786-c85c-5c00-84f0-5a881a5c7f23", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W", "pennsylvania:section": "1605.1-W", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1605.1-W"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1605.1-W", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W", "display_number": "1605.1-W", "kind": "section", "notes": ["Compiler's Note: See section 34(6)(ii) of Act 34 of 2023 in the appendix to this act for special provisions relating to continuation of prior law."], "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "source_history": ["(1605.1-W added Dec. 13, 2023, P.L.251, No.34)"]}, "ordinal": 6, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w", "parent_id": "00e7ba89-cea0-58e7-848b-416e03e5a9cc", "source_as_of": "2024-01-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1605.1-W", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFram