{"body": "This article relates to the working Pennsylvanians tax credit.\n(1601-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1601-W.2", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2/section-1601-w.2", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2025-12-03", "heading": "Scope of article", "id": "e4d786c2-5234-5a00-b5d7-c3ce9e9ff6d9", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W.2", "pennsylvania:section": "1601-W.2", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1601-W.2"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1601-W.2", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W.2", "display_number": "1601-W.2", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "source_history": ["(1601-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)"]}, "ordinal": 1, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "parent_id": "c4e231e5-9a09-53a4-8e4c-d8786fd01106", "source_as_of": "2025-12-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1601-W.2", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.2.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W.2&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "The following words and phrases when used in this article shall have the meanings given to them in this section unless the context clearly indicates otherwise:\n\"Department.\" The Department of Revenue of the Commonwealth.\n\"Federal earned income tax credit.\" The earned income tax credit provided under 26 U.S.C. \u00a7 32 (relating to earned income).\n\"Qualified taxpayer.\" A taxpayer eligible to receive a tax credit under section 1604-W.2.\n\"Tax credit.\" The working Pennsylvanians tax credit provided under this article.\n\"Tax liability.\" Tax liability under Article III of the act of March 4, 1971 (P.L.6, No.2), known as the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n\"Taxpayer.\" An individual subject to the tax under Article III of the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n(1602-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1602-W.2", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2/section-1602-w.2", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2025-12-03", "heading": "Definitions", "id": "cc0054ae-361c-5f37-b809-6390f16f7b8b", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W.2", "pennsylvania:section": "1602-W.2", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1602-W.2"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1602-W.2", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W.2", "display_number": "1602-W.2", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "source_history": ["(1602-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)"]}, "ordinal": 2, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "parent_id": "c4e231e5-9a09-53a4-8e4c-d8786fd01106", "source_as_of": "2025-12-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1602-W.2", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.2.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W.2&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "(a) Application of tax credit.--A qualified taxpayer may apply the tax credit against the qualified taxpayer's tax liability.\n(b) Spouses who file separately.--In the case of spouses who are both eligible to receive the tax credit and who file a joint Federal tax return but who elect to determine their taxes separately, the tax credit may only be used by the spouse with the greater tax otherwise due, computed without regard to the tax credit.\n(c) Amount of tax credit.--The tax credit shall be equal to 10% of the Federal earned income tax credit received by the taxpayer for the same taxable year.\n(d) Credit refundable.--If the amount of credit which the qualified taxpayer is eligible to receive under this section exceeds the qualified taxpayer's tax liability, the department shall refund the excess amount to the qualified taxpayer.\n(e) Claim of tax credit.--A qualified taxpayer shall claim a tax credit under this section on a return filed under section 330 of the act of March 4, 1971 (P.L.6, No.2), known as the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n(f) Administration of tax credit.--The administration of the tax credit under this article shall be subject to Article XVII-A.1 of the Tax Reform Code of 1971.\n(1603-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1603-W.2", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2/section-1603-w.2", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2025-12-03", "heading": "Working Pennsylvanians tax credit", "id": "d33d3a52-a1c2-548e-91b3-c68c4bea5aa3", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W.2", "pennsylvania:section": "1603-W.2", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1603-W.2"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1603-W.2", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W.2", "display_number": "1603-W.2", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "source_history": ["(1603-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)"]}, "ordinal": 3, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "parent_id": "c4e231e5-9a09-53a4-8e4c-d8786fd01106", "source_as_of": "2025-12-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1603-W.2", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.2.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W.2&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "A taxpayer is eligible to receive a tax credit if the taxpayer claimed the Federal earned income tax credit during the same taxable year.\n(1604-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1604-W.2", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2/section-1604-w.2", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2025-12-03", "heading": "Eligibility", "id": "047a1084-9302-5bf2-b6e2-1d83e3fd7c41", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W.2", "pennsylvania:section": "1604-W.2", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1604-W.2"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1604-W.2", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W.2", "display_number": "1604-W.2", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "source_history": ["(1604-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)"]}, "ordinal": 4, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "parent_id": "c4e231e5-9a09-53a4-8e4c-d8786fd01106", "source_as_of": "2025-12-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1604-W.2", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.2.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W.2&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "(a) Rules and regulations.--The department may promulgate rules and regulations to administer and enforce this article.\n(b) Guidelines.--The department may develop written guidelines for the implementation of this article. The guidelines shall be in effect until the department promulgates rules and regulations for the implementation of the provisions of this article.\n(1605-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1605-W.2", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2/section-1605-w.2", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2025-12-03", "heading": "Regulations", "id": "517e89e8-514d-59dd-939f-7d4aee006caa", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W.2", "pennsylvania:section": "1605-W.2", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1605-W.2"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1605-W.2", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W.2", "display_number": "1605-W.2", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "source_history": ["(1605-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)"]}, "ordinal": 5, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "parent_id": "c4e231e5-9a09-53a4-8e4c-d8786fd01106", "source_as_of": "2025-12-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1605-W.2", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.2.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W.2&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
{"body": "This article shall apply to taxable years beginning after December 31, 2024.\n(1606-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)", "citation_label": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1606-W.2", "citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2/section-1606-w.2", "document_class": "statute", "expression_date": "2025-12-03", "heading": "Applicability", "id": "c5275740-1772-5d16-aeb0-d5d8756c59f9", "identifiers": {"pennsylvania:act_number": "176", "pennsylvania:act_year": "1929", "pennsylvania:article": "16W.2", "pennsylvania:section": "1606-W.2", "pennsylvania:source_id": "1929-176-1606-W.2"}, "jurisdiction": "us-pa", "kind": "section", "language": "en", "legal_identifier": "The Fiscal Code \u00a7 1606-W.2", "level": 2, "metadata": {"act_number": "176", "act_year": "1929", "article": "16W.2", "display_number": "1606-W.2", "kind": "section", "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "source_history": ["(1606-W.2 added Nov. 12, 2025, P.L.156, No.45)"]}, "ordinal": 6, "parent_citation_path": "us-pa/statute/act-1929-176/article-16w.2", "parent_id": "c4e231e5-9a09-53a4-8e4c-d8786fd01106", "source_as_of": "2025-12-03", "source_format": "pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html", "source_id": "1929-176-1606-W.2", "source_path": "sources/us-pa/statute/2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2/pennsylvania-unconsolidated-statutes-html/act-1929-176/article-16w.2.html", "source_url": "https://www.palegis.us/statutes/unconsolidated/law-information/view-statute?100&iFrame=true&txtType=HTM&SessYr=1929&SessInd=0&ActNum=0176.&chpt=16W.2&subchpt=000.", "version": "2026-07-26-pa-refundable-tax-credit-statutes-us-pa-act-1929-176-articles-16w-16w.2"}
